[I] Debian/Ubuntu bootstrap scripts

[T] debootstrap installs a minimal Debian or Ubuntu base system into a
[T] subdirectory of another, already installed system, downloading the
[T] packages from a mirror. It needs no dpkg on the host and is commonly
[T] used to create chroots and install new systems from a running one.

[U] https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/debootstrap

[A] Debootstrap Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
